dsh-pet's hit area takes only the pointer: it has an accessible name, but no button role, no
tab stop and no keyboard handling. The companion A-NAS drew before this card had all three,
and the desktop is used with a keyboard too. The hit area is now a button in the tab order,
and Enter or Space on it does what a click does (a reaction, or waking the pet when it
sleeps); the card's click handler reads no event, so its prop no longer takes one.

